# Tagging rules for the post-new hook, in "notmuch tag --batch" format:
#   +tag [-tag ...] -- query
# The " -- " is required: the hook narrows each query to the mail being
# classified.  Rules run in order and later ones see earlier tags, which is
# how "bulk" leaves out what is already a list or a notification.
#
# The capitalised prefixes are mail headers declared in notmuchrc.  Mail
# carrying none of these tags is mail from people (or from a sender no rule
# knows yet -- add it here).

# Automated notifications.  GitHub's carry List-Post like a real mailing
# list, so they are claimed here first.
+notifications -- from:notifications@github.com or from:noreply@github.com or AutoSubmitted:auto

# Discussion lists: mail you could reply to the list with has List-Post.
+lists -- ListPost:mailto and not tag:notifications

# Newsletters and marketing: an unsubscribe link and no list to post to.
+bulk -- (Unsubscribe:mailto or Unsubscribe:http or Unsubscribe:https) and not tag:lists and not tag:notifications
